{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1000190-is-a-entitled-commoner-kith-presured-towards-or-a-way-from-a-house","id":1000190,"title":"Is a entitled commoner Kith presured towards or a way from a house?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-08T01:53:20-08:00","id":1000190,"title":"Is a entitled commoner Kith presured towards or a way from a house?","content":"Culturally is there more of a trend towards entitled Commoners joining or staying outside of houses? And does this vary by title level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T05:56:45-08:00","id":1000240,"title":"","content":"If a commoner is doing something impressive enough to earn a title, it seems like a noble house would definitely be recruiting her. First off, if she's skilled enough to be ennobled, her skills would give an advantage to whichever house she joins. Also, by getting as many noble fae sworn to the house as possible consolidates power within the houses. It seems to me that even the conservative houses wouldn't want a rogue noble out there acting independently and diluting the power of the houses. I'd bet they'd rather grit their teeth and bear having a commoner kith in their ranks than suffer any loss of power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:05:36-08:00","id":1000342,"title":"","content":"My assumption was always that the only way for a Commoner to become entitled was to receive a title from a House, thereby making them part of that House. I could be mistaken though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T12:40:21-08:00","id":1000383,"title":"","content":"I've seen some groups say house membership is a requirement for title. I've seen other groups say title and house membership have correlation but not causation. As long as everyone in the game is having fun, either way is correct to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T13:24:47-08:00","id":1000406,"title":"","content":"Well if only houses can give titles, no would ever have had a title before the Resurgence unless they were all Scathach. That has implications. As we know some Commoners ruled themselves prior to the Resurgence, it stands to reason they had titles of their own. Whether these titles carried the weight of the Dreaming or not ultimately depends on what you think is right for your table. Would a vote by the ruled suffice? It seems like a kind of oath, so maybe. Would conquest? That's more of a grey area, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:18:58-08:00","id":1000497,"title":"","content":"I was asking this because previously in one of our other WOD game its been heavily implied that the Lord of Washington DC is a newly Crowned Ailil. Now that we are moving into playing Changeling in the same continuity I'm enamored with the idea of a Pooka Ailil but wasn't sure how snow flakey that would be...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:05:01-08:00","id":1000729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1000190-is-a-entitled-commoner-kith-presured-towards-or-a-way-from-a-house?p=1000497#post1000497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was asking this because previously in one of our other WOD game its been heavily implied that the Lord of Washington DC is a newly Crowned Ailil. Now that we are moving into playing Changeling in the same continuity I'm enamored with the idea of a Pooka Ailil but wasn't sure how snow flakey that would be...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's perfectly fine. Go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T02:53:05-08:00","id":1001698,"title":"","content":"Tangential question but I hesitated to open a thread for it anyway. Imagine the context of a war in Concordia between Commoners and Nobles (like foreshadowed in Way of the Commoner), do you think commoner nobles will take side for nobles, commoner or it will entirely depend of the guy, as commoner nobles were depicted as a bridge between the two ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T06:50:10-08:00","id":1001736,"title":"","content":"If a civil war were to break out in Concordia, I doubt the sides would be nearly as cut and dry as they were during the Accordance War. I'd imagine it would be more along class lines than purely by kith. Landless sidhe might side more with disenfranchised Kithain while ennobled commoners might be more loyal to house than kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:43:15-08:00","id":1001915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1000190-is-a-entitled-commoner-kith-presured-towards-or-a-way-from-a-house?p=1001736#post1001736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a civil war were to break out in Concordia, I doubt the sides would be nearly as cut and dry as they were during the Accordance War. I'd imagine it would be more along class lines than purely by kith. Landless sidhe might side more with disenfranchised Kithain while ennobled commoners might be more loyal to house than kith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought there were a sizeable amount of Paper nobles in Concordia, especially for the Unseelie and second coming houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}